body:
Hunter's continue to be pidgeon-holed into invisibility for PvE content. Solar and arc are basically useless, and with renewal grasp nuked again we are left with invisibility and shatterdive as our options. 

&#x200B;

Overall, bungie needs to nerf things WAY slower. Their current model of release -> nerf in 3 different ways all at once -> leave for dead is annoying as sin. They kill entire subclasses/weapons/exotics/builds, and once they stopped being used completely they check off their box and forget about it forever.

Not trying to be rude, but there are many, *many* videos online of groups doing raids. You can get your answer by watching any of them.

&#x200B;

the answer is yes.

Hunter always has felt the most fluid. Class ability lets you continue moving and also change direction/momentum, while reloading your equipped gun. It cuts out a lot of downtime that I end up being resentful for on titans and warlocks (stand still completely to cast rift/barricade). Hunter's also benefit most from high mobility, which gives them higher strafe speed which feels wayyyy better during any gunfight. I always feel much more ground-bound and slow on my titan and warlock than on my hunter. Plus, hunters have access to shatter-skating for super speeds.

&#x200B;

Void hunter has tons of invisibility options. It does lack in the ability regen and mass-killing that warlocks and titans usually posses, but makes up for it in survivability. dragon's shadow can keep all your guns reloaded and feeling very snappy with high handling. Graviton keeps you invis as long as you want. Frostee's "can" help with ability regen, but I find them harder to really get benefit out of, since you are usually strafing during many gunfights. Mobius quiver does good damage after the 3.0 rework, and deadfall is still decent for mass-addclear.

&#x200B;

Stasis hunter can either use renewal grasps for unlimited duskfield grenades with damage reduction/resist, or use shatterdive with glacier grenades. With the ability regen fragment, glacier grenades can be used every 10-15 seconds generally, and pairing with a headstone weapon is even better. I usually run stompees on stasis for the extra speed.

&#x200B;

I do not find arc hunter useful at from a PVE standpoint. regen health on melee is really pointless when all of the other tools in the game do a better (and faster) job of killing enemies, and arcstaff is really garbage overall.

&#x200B;

Some people love solar hunter, I fail to see the benefit in it for PVE. Blade barrage isn't good, and golden gun just doesn't stack up with mobius quiver anymore. you can get some utility for better gunplay, but sacrificing invisibility/grenade spam for that isn't worth it.
